  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A small inner moon under enough tidal heating to resurface itself completely on a cycle of about four thousand years, in an episode lasting a few decades. The present surface is roughly eighteen hundred years old, which is the age of every square kilometre of it. Cryovolcanic plains of ammonia-water slush cover the whole body, and pockets of that slush stay liquid for centuries after each event.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
  ],
